      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We collected venous and capillary serum samples from 21 Zika virus\u2012infected patients on multiple days after symptom onset and found RNA load was higher and median duration of virus detection significantly longer in capillary than in venous blood. These findings raise questions about the role of the capillary compartment in virus transmission dynamics."},
